<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Democratic Party (United States)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Democratic Party is one of the two major political parties of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, organised in the 1820s around supporters of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrew-jackson">Andrew Jackson</a> and descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-jefferson">Thomas Jefferson</a>'s Democratic-Republicans. It contested elections against the Whigs and, from the 1850s, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republican-party-united-states">Republican Party</a>. In the 20th century it became the party of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-deal">New Deal</a> and of civil rights legislation, with strong support among labour unions.</p></div>
